WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.660 --> 00:00:13.963
Izzie lay on her back in the snow.

2
00:00:15.564 --> 00:00:20.085
She and Nina were making snow angels while Miss Shelly set up the Kids Central activity.

3
00:00:23.646 --> 00:00:25.347
The sky was clear and blue.

4
00:00:27.187 --> 00:00:29.708
Izzie saw a red bird land on a tree branch.

5
00:00:32.504 --> 00:00:36.325
"Tweet, tweet, tweet," she called to it.

6
00:00:36.345 --> 00:00:38.966
"Nina, don't birds eat worms and bugs?"

7
00:00:39.266 --> 00:00:39.946
Izzie asked.

8
00:00:41.426 --> 00:00:44.307
"Yes. I think so," Nina answered.

9
00:00:44.327 --> 00:00:47.988
"Then what do they eat when there is snow on the ground?"

10
00:00:49.089 --> 00:00:50.429
The girls thought about this.

11
00:00:51.549 --> 00:00:53.290
They decided to ask Miss Shelly.

12
00:00:53.310 --> 00:00:57.811
"You girls must have read my mind," Miss Shelly said.

13
00:00:57.831 --> 00:01:01.272
"I was just going to ask you that question."

14
00:01:02.272 --> 00:01:03.012
"You were?"

15
00:01:03.333 --> 00:01:03.973
Izzie said.

16
00:01:04.813 --> 00:01:06.214
Miss Shelly blew her whistle.

17
00:01:07.214 --> 00:01:10.216
Jason and Bobby stopped their snowball fight and came over.

18
00:01:10.236 --> 00:01:15.318
"Birds usually eat worms, bugs, and berries.

19
00:01:16.358 --> 00:01:18.839
But these things are hard to find in winter, right?"

20
00:01:19.220 --> 00:01:20.080
Miss Shelly said.

21
00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:22.061
"It's too cold.

22
00:01:22.681 --> 00:01:24.042
And there's so much snow!"

23
00:01:24.322 --> 00:01:24.942
Izzie said.

24
00:01:24.962 --> 00:01:28.704
"People can help birds by putting out feeders.

25
00:01:29.760 --> 00:01:34.382
Today we'll make bird feeders for the birds here on the playground," Miss Shelly said.

26
00:01:34.402 --> 00:01:37.183
"Cool!" Izzie said.

27
00:01:37.203 --> 00:01:39.204
"How do we make them?"

28
00:01:39.224 --> 00:01:43.486
"First find a pinecone by those pine trees over there."

29
00:01:44.546 --> 00:01:47.868
Miss Shelly pointed to a row of trees on the edge of the playground.

30
00:01:50.629 --> 00:01:53.730
Minutes later the kids came running back with their pinecones.

31
00:01:53.750 --> 00:01:56.471
"Mine's the biggest!"

32
00:01:56.931 --> 00:01:57.752
Bobby shouted.

33
00:02:00.900 --> 00:02:02.541
"Next choose a pipe cleaner.

34
00:02:03.221 --> 00:02:07.083
Tie one end around the stem of your pinecone," Miss Shelly said.

35
00:02:07.103 --> 00:02:11.184
"Pass me that green pipe cleaner please," Izzie said.

36
00:02:11.204 --> 00:02:14.226
"Blue please," Jason said.

37
00:02:14.246 --> 00:02:19.228
"I'm going to use a purple one," Nina said.

38
00:02:19.248 --> 00:02:23.309
"Of course you are," said Bobby.

39
00:02:23.329 --> 00:02:25.450
"What does that mean?"

40
00:02:25.930 --> 00:02:26.651
Nina asked.

41
00:02:27.771 --> 00:02:29.692
"Nothing, Miss Purple."

42
00:02:29.996 --> 00:02:30.876
Bobby grinned.

43
00:02:30.896 --> 00:02:36.239
"Now we roll the pinecones in peanut butter," Miss Shelly said.

44
00:02:40.781 --> 00:02:42.001
It's so sticky!"

45
00:02:42.021 --> 00:02:43.202
Izzie cried.

46
00:02:43.222 --> 00:02:49.624
"Exactly! We need the pinecones to be sticky so seeds will stick to them.

47
00:02:50.665 --> 00:02:53.586
Next we roll them in birdseed," Miss Shelly said.

48
00:02:53.606 --> 00:02:57.788
"It looks pretty!"

49
00:02:58.332 --> 00:03:00.353
Izzie said, holding up her pinecone.

50
00:03:01.413 --> 00:03:03.474
It was covered with different-colored seeds.

51
00:03:03.494 --> 00:03:05.614
"So does mine!"

52
00:03:06.034 --> 00:03:06.654
Nina said.

53
00:03:06.674 --> 00:03:10.596
"I hope that red bird eats from it," Izzie said.

54
00:03:10.616 --> 00:03:16.297
"Well, let's hang up your bird feeders and find out," Miss Shelly said.

55
00:03:16.317 --> 00:03:19.238
"Which tree should we hang them on?"

56
00:03:19.258 --> 00:03:21.519
"That one."

57
00:03:22.459 --> 00:03:25.820
Izzie pointed to the tree where she had seen the red bird earlier.

58
00:03:28.252 --> 00:03:31.433
Miss Shelly carried a ladder over to the tree and climbed up.

59
00:03:36.896 --> 00:03:39.217
me your bird feeders please," she said.

60
00:03:40.257 --> 00:03:43.738
Miss Shelly tied all the bird feeders onto separate branches.

61
00:03:45.919 --> 00:03:48.840
Izzie thought they looked like ornaments on a Christmas tree.

62
00:03:48.860 --> 00:03:54.443
"Now we sit, wait, and watch," Miss Shelly said.

63
00:03:55.363 --> 00:03:57.564
They sat back down at the picnic table.

64
00:03:58.568 --> 00:04:00.689
Miss Shelly poured everyone hot cocoa.

65
00:04:01.670 --> 00:04:02.891
They all watched the tree.

66
00:04:02.911 --> 00:04:05.652
"There it is!"

67
00:04:06.132 --> 00:04:07.393
Izzie whispered happily.

68
00:04:08.474 --> 00:04:10.495
Izzie pointed to a red bird in the tree.

69
00:04:11.576 --> 00:04:12.656
It hopped on a branch.

70
00:04:13.797 --> 00:04:16.338
Then it flew down to peck at Izzie's pinecone.

71
00:04:16.358 --> 00:04:20.060
"I'm going to name you Cherry," she said.

72
00:04:21.101 --> 00:04:22.962
The bird took off into the sky.

73
00:04:22.982 --> 00:04:24.523
"Good-bye, Cherry!

74
00:04:25.263 --> 00:04:26.184
Come back soon."
